config RUST_X86_PHYSADDR
	bool "Rust x86-64 physical-address validation owner"
	depends on RUST && X86_64
	default y
	help
	  Use Rust for physaddr.o, including native unsigned address arithmetic,
	  physical-width checks, sparsemem section/subsection lookup and the
	  RCU-sched lifetime. Native generated headers provide all types and
	  constants. Only compiler/preemption/lockdep/bit-access macro leaves
	  remain in the itemized companion; no pfn_valid C body is wrapped.
	  Non-extreme sparsemem, architecture-specific pfn_valid, and unsupported
	  instrumentation profiles fail explicitly in the owner rules.

config RUST_X86_RESOURCE
	bool "Rust x86-64 resource reservation owner"
	depends on RUST && X86_64
	default y
	help
	  Use Rust for resource.o, preserving BIOS/E820 clipping, unsigned
	  wraparound, tie-breaking, configured PCI policy and diagnostic text.
	  Native generated headers provide layouts, declarations and constants.
	  There is no C algorithm companion for this owner. With the reviewed
	  Clang x86-64 SMP strong stack-protector profile, an empty native
	  translation unit supplies the compiler's exact module/guard metadata
	  to strong Rust bitcode before native code generation.
	  Other stack-protector profiles, inline helpers with stack protection,
	  Clang LTO with stack protection, PRINTK_INDEX and unsupported
	  instrumentation fail explicitly. No selected profile falls back to C.
